 "method": "Each point is what the model would have said on that date using only information available then: weather observed up to that date (ERA5 / Open-Meteo analysis, mean of five peat-belt points), the ONI and DMI values published by then, and simulated weather after it. Past weather forecasts are not archived, so unlike the live odds these points do not use the 14-day forecast. Points are deterministic (fixed seed per date) and can be recomputed identically later; the series up to the build date is precomputed at build time and later days are computed on demand (at most 3 per request) and memoised in memory.",
 "computed_at": "2026-10-16T05:40:46+00:00",
 "caveats": [
  "Model odds. Not a market -- no money changes hands. Each percentage is the share of simulated seasons in which the event happened.",
  "The odds come from one statistical model fitted to 22 past seasons. Its typical error is about two weeks; the percentages include weather uncertainty and an allowance, calibrated on past seasons, for everything the model does not see.",
  "'Ended' follows the resolution definition exactly; it is about fires in the Kalimantan peat belt, not about air quality in any city."
 ],
 "build_cpu_seconds": 3.79
